{"aggregate_id": "01M3BGQ07M22KCP9XTCWSNH080", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M3BGQ089X3KWK1HAWA04209N", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-09-25T05:30:50.497425+00:00", "friendly_name": "Advancing next: task-board authority unification", "mission_id": "01M3BGQ07M22KCP9XTCWSNH080", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "advancing-next-board-unification-01M3BGQ0", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "The documented autonomous control loop (spec-kitty next --result success) is a release blocker on two P0 paths: after a reviewer rejects a work package the loop returns a success-shaped no-op forever and never re-dispatches the fix (#4980), and on the default coord topology it cannot issue a single implement step (#4975). Both are the same defect: the advancing loop derives the next step from a different, coord-blind authority than query mode uses. This mission unifies them so the loop stays trustworthy for any harness that drives it.", "purpose_tldr": "Make the autonomous spec-kitty next loop re-dispatch work after a review rejection and dispatch implement on coord missions, instead of spinning or blocking forever.", "target_branch": "fix/advancing-next-board-unification", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-09-25T05:30:50.505827+00:00"}
